Task 2.1 – Model the Events 
The Hospital Outpatient Appointment Desk uses an event-driven interface. Each component generates an event when the receptionist interacts with it. Appropriate listener interfaces handle these events.
S.No.	Event source	Event object	Listener interface	Action performed
1	Patient ID TextField	ActionEvent	ActionListener	Reads and validates the patient ID.
2	Department JComboBox	ItemEvent	ItemListener	Detects department selection and refreshes the doctor list.
3	Doctor JComboBox	ItemEvent	ItemListener	Detects the selected doctor.
4	Time Slot JComboBox	ItemEvent	ItemListener	Detects the selected appointment time.
5	Book Appointment Button	ActionEvent	ActionListener	Validates all details and books the appointment.
6	Cancel Button	ActionEvent	ActionListener	Clears the entered details or cancels the current operation.
7	Main Window	WindowEvent	WindowListener	Handles window closing and asks for confirmation if a booking is in progress.
8	Confirmation Dialog	ActionEvent	ActionListener	Confirms or cancels the closing operation.

Explanation:
- ActionEvent occurs when a button is clicked or Enter is pressed in a text field.
- ItemEvent occurs when an item in a combo box is selected or deselected.
- WindowEvent occurs when the user attempts to close the application window.
- Listener interfaces define the methods that respond to these events.
